const faqs = [
    {
        q: "How quickly can a mobile mechanic reach my location in Dubai?",
        a: "Arrival times depend on current technician availability, your specific location in Dubai, and traffic conditions along major routes such as Sheikh Zayed Road (E11) and Al Khail Road (E44). Central locations near our Al Satwa workshop are generally reached faster than outer communities. When you contact us and share your location, our team provides an estimated arrival window before dispatch."
    },
    {
        q: "What is the call-out fee for mobile car repair in Dubai?",
        a: "Our mobile call-out fee starts from AED 30 for central Dubai areas (such as Al Satwa, Jumeirah, and Business Bay). The call-out fee covers technician travel and initial assessment of your vehicle. Any required diagnostic scanning, labour, or replacement parts are itemised in a clear quotation for your approval before work begins."
    },
    {
        q: "Can a mobile mechanic repair car AC problems on-site?",
        a: "A technician can inspect AC high and low port pressures, check compressor clutch engagement, and perform a refrigerant top-up if the system holds pressure and has no severe leaks. However, major refrigerant leaks, failed compressors, condenser damage, or evaporator replacements require our Al Satwa workshop for recovery station recycling, component teardown, and leak testing."
    },
    {
        q: "What vehicle information should I provide when booking mobile service?",
        a: "To ensure we send the right tools and parts, please provide your exact parking location (building, street, or WhatsApp GPS pin), vehicle make, model, and year, along with a description of the symptoms—for example, whether the engine cranks, if dashboard lights are on, or if there are strange sounds or leaks."
